<table  width="100%" border=2 bordercolor="white" bordercolordark="white" bordercolorlight="white" cellpadding=3><tr>	<td><FONT face="Arial" size="2"><BR><B><U>Olympic News</U></B><br> <small>-<b>Shane</b> : <FONT face="Arial" size="2" color="black"><font color="#ffffff">Wednesday, October 11, 2000</small><br><br><FONT face="Arial" size="2" color="black"><b><u>WizardsRealm Leads Olympics</b></u><br><a href="http://www.wizardsrealm.com">WizardsRealm</a> currently leads in the medal Race with a score of 20 and <a href="http://www.jungleii.com">Jungle II</a> is a close second with a overall score of 17. On a side note both GameRealm Servers have been Red flagged out of the Olympics, both the Chaos and Main Server are now offically out of the Olympics. <br><br><b><u>Fountain Scroll</b></u><br>It has come to my attention that I used a graphic (The T4C Olympic Image) from the Scroll and I wanted to offer the <a href="http://www.t4cgamer.com/cytheria/t4c/Scroll/scroll.html">Fountain Scroll</a> an apology, the graphic has been removed from T4C Portal. It has also come to our attention that other sites have been using images from the scroll without giving credit, let alone asking. The Fountain Scroll is a great site and I would hope T4C fans would have more respect for the Scroll, so be more careful when grabbing screenshots and images from the Scroll.<br> <font size="-1"></td></tr></table><br>
<a name="newsitem971222185,81459,"></a>
<table  width="100%" border=2 bordercolor="white" bordercolordark="white" bordercolorlight="white" cellpadding=3><tr>	<td><FONT face="Arial" size="2"><BR><B><U>Portal looking for help</U></B><br> <small>-<b>Shane</b> : <FONT face="Arial" size="2" color="black"><font color="#ffffff">Tuesday, October 10, 2000</small><br><br><FONT face="Arial" size="2" color="black"><b><u>T4C Portal wants you!</b></u><br>We are still searching for a person to do news updates, a person who can report actual T4C News (not their own Server News)and someone who knows some html (Not for site updates but for News updates)and editing skills would be a bonus. PLEASE do not apply unless you are serious and plan on being a part of the T4C Community for a long time. If you are interested please email me at <a href="mailto:sbenson@t4cportal.com">sbenson@t4cportal.com</a>.<br><br><b><u>Site Changes</b></u><br>Please excuse the current state of the website as T4C Portal is getting a major update, the site should be back to normal by this friday.<br> <font size="-1"></td></tr></table><br>
<a name="newsitem970856410,76168,"></a>
<table  width="100%" border=2 bordercolor="white" bordercolordark="white" bordercolorlight="white" cellpadding=3><tr>	<td><FONT face="Arial" size="2"><BR><B><U>Olympic Events</U></B><br> <small>-<b>Shane</b> : <FONT face="Arial" size="2" color="black"><font color="#ffffff">Friday, October 6, 2000</small><br><br><FONT face="Arial" size="2" color="black"><b><u>Weekend Olympic Events</b></u><br><br>BUMP TRIVIA-IS BACK!!!<br><br>The Distance<br>"Because he's racing and pacing and plotting the course<br>He's fighting and biting and riding on his horse<br>He's racing and pacing and plotting the course<br>He's fighting and biting and ridding on his horse<br>He's going the distance<br>He's going for speed<br>He's going the distance "-Cake<br><br>Fri 6th<br>8PM Long Distance Lap  2 Athletes Per Heat<br>Event Overseer: MoonShadow<br><br>The Competition<br>1 lap sprint around designated path on a selected island. Server/Team<br>Members will participate. Fastest times will move on to semi and final race<br>rounds. Race clock time is the determining factor<br><br>Event Uniform Requirements: Shield<br><br>Sat 7th<br>3PM Equestrian Event (2) Person per Server Event<br>Event Overseer: Mister Ed<br>The Competition:<br>Athletes will be given horse attire to wear. Athletes will start at the<br>fountain in T1's town square. They will race to checkpoints, A B C D. This<br>will demonstrate the athlete's knowledge of Arakas as well as their speed<br>and stamina. All participants must check in at each checkpoint to win.<br>Missing a checkpoint is grounds for disqualification. A minimum of 2 team<br>members must be present for a team to compete. Any player more than 15<br>minutes late to the event will be disqualified and a red card will be<br>issued.<br>Equestrian Uniform or Weapon Required: None. Event Overseer will issue skin<br>change.<br><br>8PM Relay Race-(3) Person per Server-Team<br>Event Overseer: MoonShadow<br>The Competition<br>The track's starting line will be set in Ravens Dust at Silversky Castle and<br>will continue with 3 runner changes throughout RD. Each runner must<br>successfully drop and transfer a GM item to the next team runner, as they<br>continue throughout the race map. There will be a semi final and final<br>race-as team advance. Top three winning teams will bring home Olympic<br>medals.<br><br>Event Uniform:  Matching Team Uniforms and Shield<br><br>Sun 8th<br>3PM Olympic Feud (3) Person per Server Team<br>Event Overseer-KissyFace<br><br>The Competition:<br>Olympic Servers battle it out! Survey Says! DING!<br><br>Event Round: Wizard Realm Versus Jungle II<br><br>Event Uniform: Team MATES must match in uniform. No weapons-spell casting<br>allowed in T1 Bar and Grill.<br><br>8PM Bump Trivia-"The Game BEYOND Human Decency!"-1-3 Person per Server Event<br>Event Overseer: Nils<br><br>The Competition<br>As with all life, knowledge is key. Within the MM T4C Olympics it means<br>points. The timeless classic that has entranced AWH members for all time is<br>now being brought to the Mount Olympus. T4C Trivia at its best....jump in<br>and shout the answer but beware taking a wild guess might send you on a<br>little trip...home  May Zeus show mercy upon you. .<br><br>Event Round: Highest round tally goes to Olympic Hopeful Server<br><br>Event Uniform: None<br><br>Pantheons Crown of Olive Leaves<br>Event Overseer: None- Based on Votes from Olympiad Hopefuls<br><br>The Competition:<br>Nomination Event:<br>Pantheons Crown of Olive Leaves will be bestowed upon the noble head of the<br>event gamer that has honored his server, fellow gamers and define what is<br>meant by the use of the words-"Good Sportsmanship." One nomination per<br>person-Olympiad Hopeful. Nominations close Tues, Oct 8, 8am, PST.  Voting<br>begins-Tues-8pm. Voting details will be emailed to each Server's Olympiad<br>Hopeful. Send your nomination for Pantheon to<br>Ladywigglesnort@allwithhonor.com<br> <font size="-1"></td></tr></table><br>
<a name="newsitem970524411,71868,"></a>
<table  width="100%" border=2 bordercolor="white" bordercolordark="white" bordercolorlight="white" cellpadding=3><tr>	<td><FONT face="Arial" size="2"><BR><B><U>Olympic News</U></B><br> <small>-<b>Shane</b> : <FONT face="Arial" size="2" color="black"><font color="#ffffff">Monday, October 2, 2000</small><br><br><FONT face="Arial" size="2" color="black"><b><u>Olympic News</u></b><br><br>Today's Venues: <br><br>Monday, Oct.2 <br><br>BumpTrivia-The Game BEYOND Human Decency <br>Event Overseer-Nils <br>Unannounced "Drop-Ins" <br><br>"Olympic Bug Hunting" <br>Event Overseer-TimeViewer <br>Points based upon time stamp. <br><br>Past Events- <br><br>Sunday-Oct1 <br>Fencing (2) Per Server <br>Event Overseer: Nils <br>Final <br>Squig-Jungle II-Gold <br>Eryk-Local Link-Silver <br>Led-Wizard Realm-Bronze <br><br>Olympiad Feud-3 Olympiads per Server Required <br>DSO- Redcard (2nd Red Card) <br>GRC- Redcard (3rd Red Card) <br>Final <br>No Points <br>Honorable Mention Game Realm Chaos <br><br>Saturday-Sept30 <br>Doubles Taekwondo-2 Persons per Server Required <br>Event Overseer-Berginyan <br>Final <br>Zombais-Eryk-Local Link-Gold <br>Squigette-NightWalker-Jungle II-Silver <br>Cavalero-Fireyes-UOL-Bronze <br><br>Friday-Sept 29 <br>Singles Taekwondo-Individual Event <br>Event Overseer-Berginyan <br>Final <br>Otigon-GameRealm Chaos-Gold <br>Corellon-Wizard Realm-Silver <br>Zombais-Local Link-Bronze <br><br>Tournament Archery-2 Persons per Server Required <br>Event Overseer-Tobin <br>Final <br>Dagobah-Wizard Realm-Gold <br>Arcuturus-JungleII-Silver <br>Squigette-JungleII-Bronze <br><br>Sunday-Sept 24 <br>Olympic Bump Trivia <br>Event Overseer Nils <br>Round Winner-T4C Gamer <br><br>Roman Greco Wrestling-(1) Individual Event <br>Event Overseer: LadyWigglesnort <br>Final <br>Gold-Voldemort-Game Realm Chaos <br>Silver-Dagobah-WizardRealm <br>Bronze-Zombais-Local Link <br><br>Sat-Sept 23 <br>Opening Ceremonies <br><br>Skeet Shoot (1) Individual Event <br>Event Overseer-Tobin <br>Final: <br>Gold-Corellon-Wizard Realm <br>Silver-Night Walker-Jungle II <br>Bronze-Squigette-Jungle II <br><br>Server Red Cards Issued: <br>GameRealm-Chaos (3) <br>DragonStar Online (2) <br><br>Special Notes: <br>Due to Olympic Hopeful vote by all present-PKing will NOT be allowed. PVP is allowed in Special Arena Only Anyone PKing another-by error or intent will have their server receive ONE Red Card per PK. <br><br>GameRealm-Chaos has now been issued (3) Red Cards. Their server is out of the running the "Golden Dragon" Trophy, however-their remaining Olympiad Hopefuls have elected to keep playing for fun. <br><br>Gamers disqualified from Games of the MM T4C Olympiad: <br><br>GameRealm Chaos <br>Voldemort 09.29.00 <br>Jake 10.01.00 <br><br>T4C Olympic Medal Point Standings of Servers-Golden Dragon Placement-10.01.00 <br><br>DragonStar-----00 Pts (2) Red <br><br>GameRealm-C--06 (3) Red <br><br>GameRealm-M--00 <br><br>Jungle II Online--11 <br><br>Local Link--------07 <br><br>T4C Gamer------00 <br><br>UOL---------------01 <br><br>Wizard Realm---11 <br><br><br>Games of the MM T4C Olympiad-Olympic Village Site <br><br><a href="Http://WWW.AllWithHonor.Com">Http://WWW.AllWithHonor.Com</a> <br><br>News: <br><br>Fountain Scroll-Olympiad Edition: <br><br><a href="http://www.t4cgamer.com/cytheria/t4c/Galleries/Olympus/Olympus.html">http://www.t4cgamer.com/cytheria/t4c/Galleries/Olympus/Olympus.html</a> <br><br>T4C Portal-Frontpage: <br><br><a href="http://www.t4cportal.com/">http://www.t4cportal.com/</a> <br><br><br><br>For the Good of the Games-LW<br> <font size="-1"></td></tr></table><br>
